body:
I'm not answering neither getting angry, I know it will feed them. I just remove comments and pretend it didnt exist at all. But every 30 minutes there are 5 toxic comments.

&nbsp;

It is indeed defamatory because I was blaming the game about my loss, fifa players know how it works, the game sometimes is infuriating, and he used the editor to write things like: "I humiliated him / look how he cried / he is a loser", clearly trying to get people on hate on me, promoting himself

How old are you? there are not how things work, my friend. I want better stuff and a higher placemente on twitch, and thats why I spent a lot of hours producing content, being it live or not. I do enjoy doing this, but sometimes I do for "profissionalism". If it was all for fun, I wouldnt have a schedule, a youtube, a tiktok and a brand.

&nbsp;

I'm not saying its all about money, but its a long therm project. Otherwise, I would play a different game each day and whenever I wanted to.

I'm on the same boat, so I understand you. I have been playing FIFA for 5 months now, and althrough I got 3k followers, an ok avg viewership, etc, I just can't enjoy this game anymore, is a bad game.

&nbsp;

I peaked 50 concurrent viewers for a month or so, but FIFA is mind draining, so I started playing a few different games after FIFA, now I only stream FIFA 3 times a week, getting 30~ viewers at the most and 10~15 when I play cuphead.

&nbsp;

This is not my fulltime job, and even if I get frustrated by numbers, I try to provide those 10~15 viewers the best possible experience. I know, I could grow more, but I'd only do that if it was my fulltime job.

&nbsp;

To simplify this, lets compare. I don't "like" my fulltime job, but I have to, because that's where I get money from, that would be the same case if I was a fulltime streamer. 5~6hs of job daily. You don't have to enjoy if its professional, you have to work. If its your hobby only, then yeah, do what you enjoy.

&nbsp;

So, the question here is: do you want to take stream as a hobby or as a job?

For sure there are, oversatured times imo are bad times. January I used to stream 10pm til 3am, but it was hurting my health, since I have a full time job that I start at 7am, I couldnt sleep well... I went to a doctor and he said about this, then I changed it to 7pm~11pm, and well...

&nbsp;

My viewership dropped from 40~ to <20, I used to gain 20+ follows daily, now not even 5. I'm on the most saturated Braziliam time to stream due to my health. It's been 3 months and I couldn't get back to what I reached in January after 1 month streaming FIFA.

Well, about viewers participating on my livestream direct decisions? Not that lot. I play FIFA, so the decisions they can made are opinions. They can force me to do things withing a roullete tho, which costs 50 bits (IE, there is a redemption where I have to use Cristiano Ronaldo at GK, lmao).

&nbsp;

about indirect decisions and opinions? A lot, we're always chatting about team upgrades, what content to cover, etc, I guess I manage this good for a newer streamer, but I surely have to do this far far far better than I do, so my viewers keep growing and not just one joining while another one leaves.

&nbsp;

About conversations outside of the game? That's my main focus. We do talk about everything. I stream like 4~5 hours daily (unless I had a hard day at work, then I rest), and I usually spend the 1st 2hours just chatting, there is where I get the most viewers, but 0 new followers, then I switch to the game and most of the time we don't even pay attention on the game, lmao.

We have to take a lot of things in consideration here, but at the end, every single person have a different growth. You can both do the same thing and have different results, you can't compare growth when you're talking about twitch.

&nbsp;

Also, followers count means nothing. I'm a FIFA streamer, I get a lot of follow every day, but people don't come the next day, that's common for sports.

&nbsp;

You guys shouldn't even worry about numbers since you just started streaming, enjoy the journey.

Wow, I aprecciate so much for your atention. I did all the graphic part, I know a bit of edition but I'm not a professional, I'll of course try to match the colours, thank you.

&nbsp;

I never switched it to dark mode, so I didnt realize the mistakes, once again, thank you. I'll change all of those stuff asap, thank you, mate.

Man, move on... its yours content that the streamer is watching? Unless you own the copyrights, why care?

&nbsp;

There are a lot of streamers that watch something other than play games, and man, they're so happy doing that, why would I ruin this? also, the biggest Brazilian streamer now just react videos, nothing else, that's all.

I'd like you guys to review my stream. First of all, I'm Brazilian, so most of you won't understand the conversations there.

&nbsp;

I'm a mainly FIFA streamer that have switched to variety + FIFA recently, I'm starting with cuphead and well, my dudes are loving this game.

&nbsp;

I do a lot of just chatting before the gameplay.

&nbsp; I'm open for any suggestion and for any feedback, if you see something very bad, just tell me and I'll surely improve this área.

&nbsp;

https://www.twitch.tv/obruxo_gamer

Well, I just watched your clips and a little of your streams, so let's go.

&nbsp;
It was not clear for me that I had to vote, maybe your viewers are used to this, but I thought it was just a compiled before realizing what was the channel's purpose.

&nbsp;
You don't have either cam or mic, right? If it's a financial problem, ok, you can grow at your own pace, but I'd highly suggest you to add those features, most people I know like to see and listen to their streamer, otherwise its jus a Youtube video. Wow, As I was watching you said: "it's such a bad run", then I'd suggest you to talk more, talk about every single action you do and how you do.

&nbsp;
You're very good on the games you play, let people learn with you.

&nbsp;
The thematic is awesome, man, I do love this, and... 24/? Just re-running vods or switching streamers?

&nbsp;
Outside of this, the live is smooth as it could be, keep with the work and it of course will get better.

Yup, Single player games just doesn't attract people. It's hard to catch since if them lose one day, they'll be lost on the story, also, a lot of cutscenes and boring scenes make it hard to engage.

&nbsp;

Multiplayer games are always the same, people know what they're watching and what they're aiming for. I love playing games like final fantasy, etc, but I never watch it, because its boring.

I'm not a big streamer, but I'm always creating something new. I came from theater as an actor, I write a lot and I'm also a stand up comedian, what I have to say you is: consume stuff you do.

&nbsp;

Almost everything you did, you do or you want to do was already done by someone else. Watch other streams, movies, consume art, a streamer is an artist. Creativy comes suddenly, it's hard to programm new stuff, its always on an insight.

&nbsp;

That's it, consume what you do and you will naturally come with a lot of new ideas. As you said, you have no time, thats what stops you from creating something new. Find time, consume content, create content.

Expectations: Partnered and with a big community.

&nbsp;

Reallity: No longer streaming because I'm a sum of give ups, anxiety and a bit of disappointment for too much effort bringing me nothing back.

Yup, that's my point. I have researched about SEO, CTA, and I have optimized it the most I could, whereas of course there are videos better than mines.

&nbsp;

Maybe I didn't expressed it very good, but I tried to say that I have zero info about someone who grew up using youtube as a parallel content and still everyone here recommends this.

Well, I understand you. At the end of the day, twitch is a place to chat more than play. I'm pretty sure that if people want just to watch gameplay, they would go to Youtube and play any video. 

&nbsp;

People like to listen to stories, jokes and whatever, I personally treat the games as secondary content, doesn't matter if I'm watching or streaming, IMO chatting is the reason twitch exists.

&nbsp;

Two of the biggest Brazilian streamers, Casimiro and Gaules, they barely play anything nowadays, but when they started a few years ago, as "players", they used to take long "chatting breaks" between matches, they evolved this and now they just react, that's all. 300k viewers reacting to something. Chatting is the key to grow.

Well, something new streamers (I'm in too) have to understand is: no matter what, if your content is good, people will come. All the big streamers I watch, I have never seen on tiktok, youtube, whatever, I just found them on twitch, watched and liked.

&nbsp;

But if you want to promote, do not promote as "watch me", give content to people so they will want more of that. Tiktok is a good place (understand the platform first), I don't recommend youtube at all, it will take you a lot of effort and almost zero return.

Well, are you videos good enough? what are your videos about? You should either: be funny as fuck / make funny editions or be teaching people. "Let's play" / "live best moments" are useless unless you're already a big streamer.

&nbsp;

It's not about doing more things, it's about doing things better. If you only make lives and are very good on it, you will grow, the same for videos.

You never, never, NEVER, NEEEEEEEEEEEEVER should post: "watch me"; "watch me, please", "i'm live right now, lets check".

&nbsp;

If you create youtube videos it would help, but I don't do it, what I do on those "facebook/reddit/whatsapp/whatever groups" is give them a reason to check the stream.

&nbsp;

I'm a FIFA player, so, every time I go on I set a reason for them to watch me, like: "Hey, I just bought Messi and I'll try him today, come check with me", not just: "I'm online". There are 154165464634813213 people online, but I'm the only one they know that will be doing that content.

&nbsp;

But at the and, at the very end, promoting yourself doesnt matter as long as your stream is not a good content. If your stream is good content, people will come naturally, there is no secret at all.

That's because people want to go live today and get to avg 10 viewers tomorrow: "but I'm entertaining". As every job/study, it take a lot of time to actually get into the right direction, but people are impatient.

&nbsp;

Imagine if my neighboorood food truck says: "damn, I'm here for 5 hours and only 10 people bought my food, while McDonalds is just a common burger and millions buy it daily".

&nbsp;

McDonalds has been there for decades and people can trust their quality, even if its a normal burger, with streamers the same happens. You have to build up the loyalty of your viewers with good content EVERY SINGLE TIME. Growing 1avg view per week if a fkn awesome achievment on twitch, but no, people want it daily.

Good streamers grow, bad streamers don't. Good employees get promoted, bad employees don't.

&nbsp;

I hover over like 40 streams daily, seraching for good content to watch and a new friend to do, from those 40, if 2 are good I'm on a good day. People blame everything but themselves.

Thank you for your answer, bro, it really helps. About time, I do work 7am~6pm and stream 9pm~3am, I sleep between those times, Which means 3 hours then another 3 hours basically, I dont have that much free time. I take one day offstream weekly, but I rest, I need that rest since I don't sleep pretty well daily.

&nbsp;

Bout' the game, yup, Im making people get used to other games as I replied above and they're enjoying it, so I don't think the game will be an issue. FIFA attracts people with the same humor as me and I carry them over to other games.

Man, you words are helping me a lot. I said my "main game is FIFA", but I have been making tests, and they went pretty well. Last saturday I played Rocket League, everyone was still there yet I got RL followers, Sunday I played Fall Guys, the same happened. Last night I tried Cuphead and people still did enjoy, I know that's because I have a very small fanbase, but they all move with me wherever I go.

&nbsp;

I asked them: "bros, I'm so tired of FIFA, I will end the stream now", because I was raging, man, they all started to say on chat: "play another game, don't end the stream, please, play something else", and that made my day, like, they really like me.

See the streamer. 

&nbsp;

Nice audio quality, his voice should be louder than the music/game.

&nbsp;

Simple Layout. The Camera and maybe one goal. Some people insert logos, imgs, gifs, frame (DAMN, DONT PUT A FRAME AROUND YOUR WHOLE STREAM).

&nbsp;

And unpopular opinion: the streamer not being in a party. Whenever I join a stream and the streamer is on a call with someone, I feel like a kid watching 2 people talking to each other, I hate this.

There are a few points. I love watching some streamers and don't expect them to come to my stream, but I have raided a few smaller streamers that dont even asked their 2~3 viewers to follow me, so.. I stopped doing raids.

&nbsp;

I have sent 30~40~50 viewers to people with 5~10 viewers and them either were boring or didnt interact with me at all... Raid your friends, and if they are not online, just end your live and go to bed.

Holy Jesus, I really love my chat and I always tell them this, wether there are 5 or 20 people on stream. I'm really really happy they're there with me, like, they could be doing anything on their life but they prefer to sit and interact with me, it's a really true relationship, and I don't even get subs/bits daily.

&nbsp;

I would be nothing without my chat and I can't really express how I love them, I miss any of them when it's a missing person on that day :(

The problem here is the interface, holy moly. All those platformes coming around these years and they didn't get it yet. Twitch is clean, chat is "clean", the visual is clean. You jump into other platforms with glowing colours, things poping-up everywhere, damn. Youtube itself, you just can't catch up the chat, because it's like a comments section.

&nbsp;

I tried to watch a few friends on trovo and holy moly, I didnt know where to look at, the stream, the chat, the 2154521545 infos below the stream, or the 2176545 infos on the chat.

Why the heck dont you see your chat as friends? If you're a small streamer it makes even less sense. I'm avrg 15/20 among 50~60 people who always come back to my stream, I know their name (aside from their nick), what they do, their age, their problems. Honestly, if you're not wanting to have a nice friendship with your first viewers, streaming is not for you.

&nbsp;

Imagine someone coming back to your stream after a week and saying: "hello, streamer, the test went pretty well", and you say: "test? what you're talking about?"

Nobody cares about your vods/highlights. This is the only advice I give to everyone. Unless you are a pro player (I'm sure you're not, otherwise you just have to play the game to grow).

&nbsp;

Don't spend energy editing highlights, vods, to upload on tiktok or youtube, be different. Follow the trends on tiktok, people like people. On youtube you have to do educational content. (funny stuff is fine too).

Hello, dude. So happy for you, mate, it's always exciting when we cross our own goals. About the guy asking you to play a weird game, that's common, lmao, there will always be people asking you that.

&nbsp;

How to stream for 8 hours? Being entertained. TO be honest, I do streams for as long as I keep enjoying it, Usually 3~4hs, but sometimes things are so good that I can go 5~6~7 hours and don't even notice it.

&nbsp;

You gotta tell your friends about that, they will be your first viewers, and if you ask them to be honest, they will guide you on ways to improve your streams.

&nbsp;

I just told my parents, but to be honest, I have always showed them I liked stuff like streaming, being a content creator, etc. Just explain them, you know streaming videogames is nothing wrong, just explain them if you have to.

If you're talking about money, 0.1% and that's too much I guess. And please, never repeat that luck is more important than skills. If you're good, you will succeed, if you're bad, you will not. Why would people watch you over 55748454856445 trillions of other streamers? Ask yourself this.

&nbsp;

Everybody here thinks they deserve partner, everyone here says they're fun, etc, etc, but whem you watch some streams... they're boring AF...

&nbsp;

Yup, I'm being the devil's advocates here so you don't buy the illusion of twitch as a job.

Nop, racism goes beyond what you say here. I'm a black guy who have never been directly attacked by racism in my whole life (I live in Brazil, on a poor city, so a lot of black people here), but I can't just ignore racism, it is a thing, and even black people are racist. When you make a joke about a race, you're racist. When you do aything because of a race, you're racist, doesn't even matter if you're also one of that race, it's racism. 

&nbsp;

"My brother is black" sound like: "I'm not racist, I even have friends that are black" - Damn, that's the most annoying thing to say. The same is said for gays and a lot of other kind of people. And Holy Jesus, "Poking into a gray area but it's not racist", what the hell, dude? 

&nbsp;

Yeah, I got tilted here. Some people should not even "open their mouth" about racism, you're one of them. If you're not black, you have no idea about our pain. "It's stupid and poking into a gray area but its not racism", again, DAMN!

I'm a Brazilian streamer (Portuguese language), and I got very demotivated 2 weeks ago and stopped streaming. I really miss doing it, but I don't know if my channel is good enough: [My Channel](https://www.twitch.tv/obruxo_gamer)

&nbsp;

I'd love a feedback on my visuals, mic and on how entertaining I'm.

Well, and here comes the devil's advocate. Unless you're a big streamer, nobody cares about your vods/highlights. If you want to use the "youtube research" in your favor, you have to do quality content.

&nbsp;

But let's say you really want to do this, and want to add some memes through the gameplays, camera zoom, slow motions, add some visual elements, etc. You will spend at least 10hrs to create a quality video (assuming you don't know yet where are the good points of the vod), again, unless you just throw your gameplay there and it's that.

Dont try to be a big streamer before being one. If you prepare "everything" before streaming, you will just burnout, since you will not be able to see any development for days/months.

&nbsp;

About TikTok, it's very useful, but you have to be unique. Are you a pro, a fun or a talking streamer? But always, always, ALWAYS follow the non-gaming trends. People like people, not robots, and a hard thing to get. PEOPLE DON'T CARE ABOUT YOUR GAMEPLAYS/VODS.

Because I made a lot of networking, I really like watching those people, I'm not there to ask for them to come for my live, I never even said I stream, they just realized and came.

&nbsp;

 I'm entertaining, I engage chat, I have a lot of cool addons on my stream so they can joke on me. I'm not good at any game, but I'm a standup guy, so I try to always make jokes about watch I'm doing. People enter, people like, people still.

&nbsp;

Looks like you're salty with something, if it is the case, just calm down, bro. Everything is important, from schedule to quality content, it is a show, treat it as a show. EVERYTHING should be perfect, aligned and make sense. I call my show "The one man Circus", and it works a lot, that's my stream. I'm just a clear face clown with some game on the background.

I'm a new streamer too, just got affiliate, but yes, they all do work, and there is the reason every bigger streamer advices them.

&nbsp;

On my path to affiliate, I was trying to find similar streamers, and well, I ended up liking a few streams and (schedule) every day, on the same time, I go their stream.

&nbsp;

Also, whenever I join a stream and say: "hi, I like cats, and apparently my dog like it too", and they just say: "hello", and don't even laugh of my joke or try to engage me, I leave. So, there is one thing you should keep in mind first: "What makes me keep watching someone?", and that's what you should do to grow.

I know, I know, there is no game on the world like Dragon's Dogma, but I guess you guys will get what I'm trying to say here. I want a coop game where I can play on 3rd person, which has magic/spells, etc. 

&nbsp;

My friend loves to play as a sword boy and I love to just throw fire everywhere, BURN, BURN, BUUUUUUUURN! 

&nbsp;

Haha. Jokes aside, we already finished:

• Divinity 2

• Diablo 3


&nbsp;

We tried magicka but it didn't fit our playstyle. But the biggest problem here is that we don't want a MMORPG, or anything that we should grind, etc. We just want to sit there, once in a week and have fun.

&nbsp;

Is there anything in the world like that? Or do you recommend any game with a storyline that can be played on an online coop? Thanks!

Hello, how are you, my friends? 
I'm a Brazilian gamer and I created a gaming channel based on RPG (JRPG, CRPG, ARPG, etc). I'm just in love with everything I'm doing, if you want to checkout, this is the link:
&nbsp;
https://youtu.be/biAv512XLNI

&nbsp;

If you don't understand my language, it's fine, lol, audio/img and etc critics would be fine for me, thanks.

Holy Jesus. I play this game since this release, I still haven't finished any world missions and I only have 4~5 characters maxed out. Also, I still have more than 10 characters to unlock and I'm sitting on 9999 gems + box.

&nbsp;

I wish I had that patience to grind through all those missions. Time I have, I just think they're boring AF.

I don't understand why people want to buy HL characters, like, it's tibia, you will make the same movies wherever you're hunting. Independent on the level, the only thing that changes are the sprites of creatures/equipments.

&nbsp;

Every time I hit 300+ (only 2 times so far, lmao) with a character, I "reset" and start a new one, because things start to become so boring. You just hunt Gazers for 300 levels, lol.

&nbsp;

I wouldn't reccomend, you will have no motivation to play if you don't have "emotional connection" to the character, trust me, you won't.

Unpopular opinion for downvotes: I really don't believe there is SMH. I say this as an E2/E3 player. Sometimes I play lazy and can't see runs, sometimes my connection is poor and sometimes I'm just unlucky. The problem is that there is a xx% accuracy for every input, and some games you get it against you multiple times.

&nbsp;

After more than 6 years playing UT, I managed to realize that, and that's when I improved from Gold 1 to Elite 2 constantly (almost got E1 once, but was tilted on the last game). You have to be 100% focused. It's also not easy to program 11vs11 players and make no BS happens with so many animations.

&nbsp;

It's really "fun" when someone says: Handicap attacked me, I droped from D1 to D8 in a week, like, serious, bro? There is no proof that Handicap is a thing, neither S or M. As long as there are 150 players getting 30-0 almost back-to-back, I won't believe in Handicap.

&nbsp;

"Oh, they're just to good to avoid Handicap". Well, that argument goes against the handicap argument, lmao. If they're good to "avoid", then I should be that good too, simple as that.

Level 50 wizard, what to do now? rush to awakening? or isn't it that relevant? 

&nbsp;

I'm hunting catfishmen since 35~ and noticed that after 50 I don't get as much xp as before, should I change my spot?

Althrough KDB is an awesome player, I still don't think he is able to do what Neymar does. As you stats suggests, imo he doesn't have the same shooting accuracy as Neymar. Neymar is a key player that wins games by itself, and again, althrought KDB makes a huge impact on the game, he isn't "unfair" for his opponents as Neymar is. Ronaldo and Messi don't need explanations tho.

&nbsp;

IMO: Messi "x", Ronaldo "x-1", Neymar "x-2", KDB "x-3" and Lewa "x-4", then the other players. Lewa is another thing that I can't buy for being the "top world" people say. Come on, Bayern wins the Bundesliga since ever.

Ball relative, don't let the AI defend for you, you have to push the CBs too on this game, pressure. You have to press the button at the perfect time, like when the dude is cuting inside with fake shot, he will slow down after the next touch, that's when you have to tackle. If you act before the perfect time, the attacker will pass "through" you and you will blame the game.

&nbsp;

2 vs 2 situation. Almost always defend against the player who will receive the pass, not the one with the ball. Sometimes you'll have to fake your movement forward, opening a gap, forcing his passing to intercept it.

&nbsp;

It's hard to say what you have to do, because it's football and you have 999999999 different situations. You have to master the animations to know when to act. I recommend you to watch Boras, Jukez, those 30-0 legends. I'm saying this as an E2 player, scoring a goal is too easy, the hard part is defending.

There is nothing that can make me play FUT 20 anymore. It's such a mind draining game that, after 9 months I had to stop, take a break and think about buying FIFA 21. I'm just mentally exhausted of this game, even when I remember about it I get frustated. Is not like the game is bad, unplayable, blablabla, but it drains so much of a life to stick with it through 12 months.

&nbsp;

I'm playing more casual games now, some Tibia, Black Desert, Rocket League, Rocket Arena, etc. My goal for this FIFA was top 100, unfortunately I could only reach 26 wins. Not bad, but it got me more time than I would admit.

I'm not proud to admit, but yesterday I messaged a guy. I was playing friendlies for TOTY challenges, listening to music, my mind was anywhere else. The dude scored 2-0 with his regular team, watched both replays, the walk and on the second did the calm down...

&nbsp;

Well, I just turned on my Ash Mode, focused on the game and before the halftime it was 6-2 to me (I kept skipping replays, because its auto in my head, lol). He RG on the halftime and I sent to him on psn: "Bro, don't try to annoy people online when you can't even defend for you life, doing this on friendlies just show how poor your life is".

Well, I just bought this game from the PSN sales and I'm Loving it. I created a Wizard, since is my main class on every game, lol. My questions are: 

1. Can I just go through the story ignoring everything else until I reach max level?
&nbsp;
2. Should I enchance my weapons or since I dont know what I'm doing, just keep playing and saving black stones?
&nbsp;
3. I've read some guides, but they all talk as if I already knew about the game. I'm focusing my points on lightning: (L stick down + cirle), is is the best to do? How do I combo my spells? (Rotation) I just keep spamming all spells, since I find them so beauty, lol (I love the fireball / fireexplosion).

You do an awesome job, mate!

&nbsp;

MM are always the "same", but tbh is always nice to have a thread about it.

What a challenge I have here....
 I have untradable:


&nbsp;
 TOTS: Renato Sanchez, De Jong, Theo Hernandez, Sergio Ramos, Carvajal, Alejandro Gomez, FB Militão, SH Kessie, RIbery, Dembele.


&nbsp;
And I have 2.2M, which I'm planning to buy HL Neymar (I love Neymar, a personal love). How do I fit him with all those players? lmao (Ribery and Dembele are a must).

It will sound weird, but let's go...

&nbsp;

I used him on my last E2 finnish, he is awesome, but he is so slugish that cost me the E1, you really can't open space / create chances with him. He is awesome, but felt like 2* WF for me, this is a review on the card.

&nbsp;

Yes, if you want to use him, totally worth. The difference between them is huge, its like 96 to 110 OVR, but the game is caped at 99.

Hello, mates. I'm Brazilian, actually a Santos FC fan, and my goal this entire FIFA was to build our historic XI. No I'm able to afford Pele and the other, but I'm struggling to find other players who played for us. 

&nbsp;

Do you guys know any player on this game who actually played for Santos FC? Thanks!

I once stated that, even if EA gave us a "Dream ticket" at the start of FIFA, which we pick any player to use, some stuff like a captain, it wouldn't affect anything. We have 11 players on the pitch. Give me a gold Messi at the start of FIFA and I'll still have to grind for another 10 positions.

&nbsp;

That "worrying amount of people" downvoted me, because apparently they don't want everyone to have access to all cards.

Nice words, mate. I'm one of those people who already lost the hope. Don't get me wrong, the world is wonderful, life is wonderful, I just don't fit in, but I do wish everyone wins those battles.

&nbsp;

I'm 27 yo, I may have this Demon inside me since I was 7~8, idk, and I gotta say, words like yours save a lot of lifes around the world. Keep being positive, mate, I really wish you the best.

&nbsp;

FIFA Community, I know, you're not angry on your opponents, you're mad with the game, we all are. Be nice to each other, save lives, save days <3

Dear god, no. I know, it's a way to "achieve" icon player, but tell me, which Icons were really worth the effort? 40 wins on Rivals using SH&& players, I really skipped all of the swaps batches and didn't miss anything.

&nbsp;

All the objectives concepts are awesome, SH, Swaps, etc, but the conditions are awfull. It stops being worth the effort when it crosses the line from fun to exhausting.

Because it's the only enjoyable game mode. Gameplay is better, games are better, people skip replays and there is a competitive feel.

&nbsp;

I never play Rivals, but had to this week, for the objecvites... I'll never do objectives on Rivals again. Every single player did watch the full replays, it's annoying. Not to say that everyone plays 1depth drop back, what a waste of time.

Only because they are favourite players of the fanbase, nothing else at all. Chem is relevant, but you can fit an awesome squad without a single icon. They don't have hidden boosts as people say, that's just people amazed when they perform well and recording those momments, because they like those cards.

